{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>And I will meet there with the children of Israel, and it shall be sanctified, etc.</b> One needs to know the verse's intention — what does it come to teach us by saying <b>and I will meet there with the children of Israel</b>? It would appear that it comes to give a reason for what He says at the conclusion of His words — <b>and it shall be sanctified in My glory</b> — and they of blessed memory said (Zevaḥim 115b) that here it is stated to Moses, ״בִּקְרֹבַי אֶקָּדֵשׁ״ (Leviticus 10:3). Therefore He prefaced by saying <b>and I will meet there with the children of Israel</b> — meaning, since I summon My Shekhinah to the children of Israel, I am concerned for them lest there be a breach of the fence and a diminution of glory on their part; therefore it is necessary to sanctify it through those near Me, so that they will fear My sanctuary. And He hinted to him that there was no need to do anything except on account of Israel, but as for Himself, He has no need for this sanction."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:32.064953709Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}